# Template. Copy to mcuboot-key.conf and point it at the real key.
#
# PLACEHOLDER ONLY, generated by blanking the value rather than by copying a
# working file.
#
# This is the APPLICATION half: the key imgtool signs the image with. It must
# name the same key the bootloader was built to verify against. If it does not,
# the bootloader simply refuses the image - a visible, safe failure, which is
# why this half carries no fail-closed guard while the bootloader's does.
CONFIG_MCUBOOT_SIGNATURE_KEY_FILE=""
